/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig
node_modules/
/crates/app/frontend/dist/

# Local sidecar / env
.env
.env.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code session state and the linked worktrees under `.claude/worktrees/` — never
# commit these, they hold whole checkouts and their build output.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git will not look inside an excluded *directory*, so
# the negation below cannot rescue anything if the directory itself is the pattern.
.claude/*
# ...except skills. A checked-in prompt is source — it is how the team shares one.
!.claude/skills/

# A Mini-Me copy assembled by scripts/bundle-backend.sh for a packaged build. Still not
# tracked — it is build output, not source.
#
# The source itself now lives at `mini-me/` **and is tracked**. That reverses §5's "bundled,
# never forked", on the researcher's instruction: *"from now I want a mono repo in mini me
# desktop. I dont want to depende on a secod repo anymmore."* See docs §135 for what the old
# rule was protecting and why it stopped being worth its cost.
/vendor/

# Python bytecode from the overlay, which the *backend* regenerates every run. Tracking
# these made `git pull` abort with "local changes would be overwritten" on the one machine
# that actually runs the backend — the user's.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/dist/

# The LangGraph server's own state directory, written into whatever checkout the backend runs
# from. It holds the conversation index (`.langgraph_ops.pckl`) and the copies `index_guard`
# keeps beside it, which are runtime data for one machine and mean nothing on another. Five of
# those copies reached `main` in #76 because this line was missing.
.langgraph_api/
